.TH UH7000-PANEL 1 "July 2026" "tascam-uh7000-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uh7000-panel \- graphical status and control panel for the TASCAM UH-7000
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uh7000-panel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uh7000-panel
opens the Qt Quick session-bus client for
.BR uh7000d (1).
It displays the detected USB configuration, ALSA topology, verified clock
source, and safety state. Controls without capture, readback, and rollback
evidence are intentionally unavailable.
.PP
The panel requires a graphical session with the Qt Quick runtime installed by
the Debian package dependencies.
.SH SAFETY
Do not use diagnostic playback with speakers or headphones connected. The
panel does not bypass the command-line playback safety gates, and unknown
direct-monitor state is treated as unsafe.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uh7000d (1),
.BR uh7000ctl (1),
.BR uh7000-pipewire (1)
